  <layout>One page of verse in one column, centred on the text block; running head "EPITAPHIA." at the top; page number 64 at the top right. No marginal notes beyond small scan specks.</layout>
  <page_number>64</page_number>
  <running_head>EPITAPHIA.</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" para="true">Leuiane, planxero?</l>
    <l n="2" para="true">
      <i>Iam dextrus pares tuis,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="3" para="true">
      <i>Doloribus pares meis,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="4" para="true">
      <i>Vestus modòsque flebiles,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="5" para="true">
      <i>Non pectus hoc suggesserit,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="6" para="true">
      <i>Non istud os effuderit,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="7" para="true">
      <i>Non ergo Beza te tuus,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="8" para="true">
      <i>Leuiane, planxerit?</i>
    </l>
    <l n="9" para="true">
      <i>Mirabit immo quandiu</i>
    </l>
    <l n="10" para="true">
      <i>Te Beza flebit tamdiu,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="11" para="true">
      <i>Donec ipsa quàm mihi</i>
    </l>
    <l n="12" para="true">
      <i>Leuianum sustulit,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="13" para="true">
      <i>Leuiano me meo</i>
    </l>
    <l n="14" para="true">
      <i>Vnita iungat redditum.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="15" para="true">
      <i>Aleftem Et intra regiam,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="16" para="true">
      <i>Qua iam tui parte altera,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="17" para="true">
      <i>Christo potitus es duce,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="18" para="true">
      <i>Vt Beza, quò nunc gestiens</i>
    </l>
    <l n="19" para="true">
      <i>Magnis anhelat passibus,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="20" para="true">
      <i>Certis Et terque iubilis,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="21" para="true">
      <i>Festinemus haec suspiria,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="22" para="true">
      <i>Serennibúsque gaudiis</i>
    </l>
    <l n="23" para="true">
      <i>Iam obruamus lacrymas.</i>
    </l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Verse is printed in long lines with a slightly irregular left edge; several words are blurred by the scan (e.g. "Iam dextrus", "Vestus", "Donec ipsa quàm", "Festinemus", "Serennibúsque") and the readings of those words are doubtful. The first line is partly obscured by a marginal mark near "planxero".</notes>
